Modified by Moshpit (Cluas), 2026-11-11:
- terminal-emulator/.../TerminalSession.java is replaced: instead of running
  a local process on a pseudo-terminal (JNI.createSubprocess, two I/O threads
  and one main-thread message per 4 KB read), a session writes to and is fed
  by a Transport, the app's byte channel to its Rust core. Termux's public
  surface (getEmulator, updateSize, write, writeCodePoint, the client
  callbacks) and its UTF-8 encoding of code points are kept.
- terminal-emulator/.../TerminalEmulator.java eats screen's window title
  sequence (ESC k ... ST) as it eats APC (2026-11-12): a tmux -CC client gets
  a pane's bytes raw, and a shell in tmux sets its title that way, which was
  printed into the pane.
- terminal-emulator/.../JNI.java, ByteQueue.java and src/main/jni (the pty
  and process natives, libtermux.so) are removed: nothing uses them.
- The scripted build has no AndroidX: androidx.annotation.Nullable and
  RequiresApi come from compile-time stand-ins in androidx-stubs/ (the
  Gradle build uses the real androidx.annotation).
- Each library has a build.gradle of its own (Android library modules of
  android/settings.gradle), as in termux-app.
